# Copy to .env.local and restart the dev server.
# The same server-side coach configuration is read by /api/coach, /api/career, and /api/builder.
# The key stays on the server. Never put it in client code or send it to the browser.
# Leave the key empty, or set PROVIDER=local, to use the local rubric and local templates.
# A placeholder key is treated as no key and is not sent.
# Gemini calls the Developer API at generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta.
# Create a key in Google AI Studio (aistudio.google.com/apikey).
# This app does not require the key to start with a particular prefix.
# Set MODEL to a real model ID from that project. A placeholder such as YOUR_MODEL_ID,
# or an empty MODEL when PROVIDER=gemini, stays local and is not sent.
# Leave application restrictions off so this server can call the API.
# Leave BASE_URL empty to use https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta.
# This app does not enable billing. There is no paid fallback.

INTERVIEWVERSE_COACH_PROVIDER=gemini
INTERVIEWVERSE_COACH_API_KEY=
INTERVIEWVERSE_COACH_MODEL=
INTERVIEWVERSE_COACH_BASE_URL=
